# Project Workflow

- Use GitHub issues to track feature and hardening work. Close issues only when the scoped work is implemented and validation is known.
- Keep changes small and reviewable. Prefer focused passes over broad rewrites.
- Do not revert user changes or generated local work unless explicitly asked.
- Before committing, inspect status, diff, and recent commit style. Do not skip hooks unless the user explicitly asks.
- When npm is unavailable in the agent environment, rely on the user's local `npm run lint`, `npm run test`, and `npm run build` confirmation.
- Preserve the current plain-CSS, Sleeper-first, React + TypeScript architecture unless an issue explicitly changes direction.
